<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:app="clr-namespace:EmberTern.App"
             xmlns:controls="clr-namespace:EmberTern.App.Controls"
             xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:EmberTern.App.ViewModels"
             xmlns:conv="clr-namespace:EmberTern.App.Converters"
             xmlns:ae="using:AvaloniaEdit"

             x:Name="ImportRoot"
             x:Class="EmberTern.App.Views.DataImportTabView"
             x:DataType="vm:DataImportTabViewModel"
             Background="{DynamicResource BackgroundBrush}">

  <!--
    Data Import — ONE working surface with collapsible sections, deliberately NOT a wizard (decision D7).

    ⭐ LAYOUT, ratified 2026-07-26 after the first visual review of I5 (§3.8). Two things drive it:

    1. THE STAR BELONGS TO THE WORK, NOT TO THE CONFIGURATION. Until this review the configuration
       ScrollViewer was the '*' row and the preview was nailed to 190 px — backwards, and the reason the
       preview was "practically invisible". Configuration has a natural size and folds away; mapping and
       preview are where the user spends the session, so they get every pixel that is left.

    2. THE SECTIONS SPLIT BY HOW OFTEN A DECISION CHANGES, not by subject. The file (and later the target
       table) changes on every run and therefore stays live at all times; the separator/encoding/date format
       are set once and fold away. Collapsing the picker with them would make the commonest action in the
       module cost an expand + a collapse, and §1.2 promises a repeat import is one F5.

    Bands are §3.1's. Band A (the "Data Import" header) was REMOVED — no other EmberTern module carries one
    and the tab title already says it; the one fact it was supposed to carry (connection + lane) moved to
    band H, where the transaction mode joins it in I7.

    Etap I5 delivers C, D, E1, F(empty state), G and H. The command bar (B) and the target tile (E2) have
    their rows reserved here so I6/I7 drop in rather than restructure — but nothing renders in them yet: an
    enabled-looking control with nothing behind it would be a lie the readiness strip could not correct.
  -->

  <!--
    ⚠ The work row deliberately has NO MinHeight, and that is a user decision (2026-07-27), not an oversight.

    A floor was added here to close §3.8/U5 — in the „New table" variant the Target tile is the tallest band on
    the surface, so the star row could be squeezed to nothing. Seen running, the cure read worse than the
    disease: honouring the floor forced the bottom panel to give way, the middle of the window became too tall,
    and the bottom panel stopped being useful. The user reverted it and ratified where the real fix belongs —
    the app-wide UX sprint, where control heights come down and the surface regains the ~100 px that make this
    a non-problem. **Do not re-add a floor here, and do not answer the height problem by adding another
    vertical section.** U5 is OPEN again, on purpose, and belongs to that sprint.
  -->
  <Grid x:Name="SurfaceLayout" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,*,Auto,Auto,Auto">

    <!-- ══ Band C — the ONE message surface. Never a locally-coloured TextBlock (§9.1 point 5). ══ -->
    <controls:MessageBanner Grid.Row="0"
                            Classes="docked"
                            Severity="{Binding StatusSeverity}"
                            Message="{Binding StatusMessage}"
                            IsVisible="{Binding HasStatusMessage}" />

    <!-- ══ Band B — command bar (§3.1) ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         The timer is DOCKED RIGHT, outside the button panel, so a running import never shifts the
         buttons under the pointer — the Script Executor's pattern, reused rather than re-invented. -->
    <Border Grid.Row="1" Background="{DynamicResource PanelBrush}"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="0,0,0,1" Padding="12,6">
      <DockPanel LastChildFill="True">

        <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Right" Text="{Binding Timer.ElapsedDisplay}" FontSize="11"
                   FontFamily="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" Margin="8,0,4,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}"
                   IsVisible="{Binding Timer.IsRunning}" />

        <!-- The live counters sit beside the timer, so "what is happening" reads as one thing. -->
        <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Right" Text="{Binding ProgressText}" FontSize="12"
                   Margin="8,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}"
                   IsVisible="{Binding IsRunning}" />
        <!-- Indeterminate when the row count is unknown: a streaming import cannot know it without reading
             the file twice, and inventing a percentage would be a number that is not true. -->
        <ProgressBar DockPanel.Dock="Right" Width="140" Height="6" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                     Minimum="0" Maximum="100" Value="{Binding ProgressPercent}"
                     IsIndeterminate="{Binding IsProgressIndeterminate}"
                     IsVisible="{Binding IsRunning}" />

        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" VerticalAlignment="Center">

          <!-- ══ Named profiles (etap I11) ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
               ⭐ This is the slot §4.8.4 reserved back in the MVP — the leftmost position of band B, before
               Importuj — precisely so that adding the selector would not rearrange the toolbar. It did not:
               everything to the right of this block is untouched.

               The selector carries its own scope sentence as a tooltip, because the list deliberately does NOT
               show profiles saved on other connections and a restriction the user cannot see is
               indistinguishable from a profile that has gone missing. -->
          <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportProfileLabel}" Classes="field-label"
                     VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0" />
          <ComboBox x:Name="ProfilePicker" MinWidth="170" VerticalAlignment="Center" FontSize="12"
                    ItemsSource="{Binding Profiles}"
                    SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedProfile, Mode=TwoWay}"
                    IsEnabled="{Binding IsConfigurationEnabled}"
                    ToolTip.Tip="{Binding ProfileScopeNote}">
            <ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
              <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ImportProfileRowViewModel">
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Display}" FontSize="12" />
              </DataTemplate>
            </ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
          </ComboBox>

          <Button Classes="flat" Command="{Binding SaveProfileAsCommand}"
                  IsEnabled="{Binding IsConfigurationEnabled}"
                  Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportProfileSaveAs}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportProfileSaveAsTooltip}" />

          <!-- Rename and delete act on the SELECTED profile, so they are icon-only secondary actions and
               disable themselves when there is nothing selected — their CanExecute says so, not a binding here. -->
          <Button Classes="icon" Command="{Binding RenameProfileCommand}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportProfileRenameTooltip}">
            <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.Pencil}"
                              Foreground="{DynamicResource AccentIconBrush}" />
          </Button>
          <Button Classes="icon" Command="{Binding DeleteProfileCommand}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportProfileDeleteTooltip}">
            <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.Trash}"
                              Foreground="{DynamicResource DangerIconBrush}" />
          </Button>

          <!-- Reset belongs on THIS side of the divider: it is about the configuration as a whole and it
               detaches the profile, so it is part of managing profiles, not of running an import. Labelled
               rather than icon-only because the user's report was that they could not find a way to do it —
               an unlabelled glyph would not have fixed that. -->
          <Button Classes="flat" Command="{Binding ResetConfigurationCommand}"
                  IsEnabled="{Binding IsConfigurationEnabled}"
                  Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReset}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportResetTooltip}" />

          <!-- ⭐ The bar's PRINCIPAL boundary: managing the configuration on the left, running it on the right.
               Deliberately wider than the separator further right (which only divides settings WITHIN the
               execution group), because these two groups are not peers — a profile is superordinate to the whole
               import configuration, so its break should read as the stronger of the two. -->
          <Border Width="1" Margin="12,2" Background="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" />

          <Button Classes="primary" Command="{Binding ImportCommand}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportRunTooltip}">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
              <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.Import}" Width="14" Height="14"
                                Foreground="{DynamicResource OnAccentBrush}" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportRun}" />
            </StackPanel>
          </Button>

          <Button Classes="flat" Command="{Binding ValidateCommand}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportValidateTooltip}">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
              <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.Check}" Width="14" Height="14"
                                Foreground="{DynamicResource SuccessIconBrush}" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportValidate}" />
            </StackPanel>
          </Button>

          <!-- ⭐ Refresh sits with the other surface-level actions, not by the file picker, because it re-reads
               every fact the surface holds — the source, the table list AND the target — and then re-runs the one
               recalculation chain. Icon only: it is a secondary action beside Import and Validate, and the shared
               refresh mark (used by the metadata tree, Session Manager and Table Data) already says what it does. -->
          <Button Classes="icon" Command="{Binding RefreshCommand}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportRefreshTooltip}">
            <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.RefreshCw}"
                              Foreground="{DynamicResource AccentIconBrush}" />
          </Button>

          <!-- Only visible while there is something to cancel: a permanently disabled Stop teaches nothing. -->
          <Button Classes="icon" Command="{Binding CancelRunCommand}"
                  IsVisible="{Binding IsRunning}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportCancelTooltip}">
            <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.Stop}" Foreground="{DynamicResource DangerIconBrush}" />
          </Button>

          <!-- ⭐ Commit / Rollback live HERE, in the top command bar beside Import and Validate.
               Every main action in EmberTern is taken from the top toolbar, and after an import the
               transaction decision IS a main action — it was previously only in the Report tab, where it
               read as a footnote while a red "transaction is open" line read as a failure. They appear only
               once THIS module's run has left a transaction open, so the buttons never offer to commit work
               the import did not do. -->
          <Border Width="1" Margin="4,2" Background="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}"
                  IsVisible="{Binding Report.TransactionLeftOpen}" />

          <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTransactionOpenMarker}"
                     VerticalAlignment="Center" FontSize="12"
                     Foreground="{DynamicResource WarningBrush}"
                     ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTransactionOpenMarkerTooltip}"
                     IsVisible="{Binding Report.TransactionLeftOpen}" />

          <Button Classes="flat" Command="{Binding CommitCommand}"
                  IsVisible="{Binding Report.TransactionLeftOpen}"
                  IsEnabled="{Binding !IsRunning}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportCommitTooltip}">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
              <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.Check}" Width="14" Height="14"
                                Foreground="{DynamicResource SuccessIconBrush}" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportCommit}" />
            </StackPanel>
          </Button>
          <Button Classes="flat" Command="{Binding RollbackCommand}"
                  IsVisible="{Binding Report.TransactionLeftOpen}"
                  IsEnabled="{Binding !IsRunning}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportRollbackTooltip}">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
              <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.Undo}" Width="14" Height="14"
                                Foreground="{DynamicResource DangerIconBrush}" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportRollback}" />
            </StackPanel>
          </Button>

          <Border Width="1" Margin="4,2" Background="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" />

          <!-- The mode carries its consequence as a tooltip, where the decision is taken (§0.5) — the
               Script Executor's `Sequenced` precedent. -->
          <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTransactionLabel}" Classes="field-label"
                     VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0" />
          <ComboBox x:Name="TransactionModePicker" SelectedIndex="{Binding TransactionModeIndex, Mode=TwoWay}" MinWidth="170"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center" FontSize="12"
                    IsEnabled="{Binding IsConfigurationEnabled}"
                    ToolTip.Tip="{Binding TransactionModeDescription}">
            <ComboBoxItem Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTransactionManual}" />
            <ComboBoxItem Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTransactionAutoCommit}" />
            <ComboBoxItem Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTransactionBatched}" />
          </ComboBox>

          <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportErrorPolicyLabel}" Classes="field-label"
                     VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0" />
          <ComboBox SelectedIndex="{Binding ErrorPolicyIndex, Mode=TwoWay}" MinWidth="180"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center" FontSize="12"
                    IsEnabled="{Binding IsConfigurationEnabled}">
            <ComboBoxItem Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportErrorPolicyStop}" />
            <ComboBoxItem Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportErrorPolicySkip}" />
          </ComboBox>
        </StackPanel>
      </DockPanel>
    </Border>

    <!-- ══ Band D — readiness strip: every gap at once, each one clickable to its cause ══════════ -->
    <Border Grid.Row="2" Background="{DynamicResource PanelBrush}"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="0,0,0,1" Padding="12,5">
      <StackPanel Spacing="4">

        <!-- The chips: one per section, ✓ when the section has nothing to say. These carry §3.2's promise
             that every gap is visible at once — which is what lets the findings below be capped. -->
        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="14">
          <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReadinessHeader}"
                     Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
          <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Readiness.Sections}">
            <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
              <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="14" />
              </ItemsPanelTemplate>
            </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
              <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ImportReadinessSectionViewModel">
                <!-- A chip is a status light AND a way in: it shows the section's state and takes the
                     user there. One behaviour for all five, so the row can be read rather than learned. -->
                <Button Classes="flat" Padding="4,2"
                        ToolTip.Tip="{Binding FocusHint}"
                        Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:DataImportTabViewModel)DataContext).FocusSectionCommand}"
                        CommandParameter="{Binding Section}">
                  <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="5">
                    <!-- A brush is looked up WITH the theme variant, never without: a variant-less lookup
                         returns UNSET and the icon then paints nothing while every state looks healthy
                         (gotcha #250). -->
                    <controls:SvgIcon Width="13" Height="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                      Data="{Binding GeometryKey, Converter={x:Static app:IconGeometryConverter.Instance}}">
                      <controls:SvgIcon.Foreground>
                        <MultiBinding Converter="{x:Static app:IconBrushConverter.Instance}">
                          <Binding Path="BrushKey" />
                          <Binding ElementName="ImportRoot" Path="ActualThemeVariant" />
                        </MultiBinding>
                      </controls:SvgIcon.Foreground>
                    </controls:SvgIcon>
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Title}" FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                  </StackPanel>
                </Button>
              </DataTemplate>
            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
          </ItemsControl>
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- When everything is green the strip collapses to one line (§3.2). -->
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding Readiness.Summary}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="12"
                   IsVisible="{Binding !Readiness.HasItems}" />

        <!-- The findings — CAPPED (U6). Bound to VisibleItems, never Items: the cap is the VM's decision and
             the view must not be a second place that decides how much to show. -->
        <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Readiness.VisibleItems}" IsVisible="{Binding Readiness.HasItems}">
          <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ImportReadinessItemViewModel">
              <Button Classes="flat" Padding="2,1" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                      ToolTip.Tip="{Binding Code}"
                      Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:DataImportTabViewModel)DataContext).FocusSectionCommand}"
                      CommandParameter="{Binding Section}">
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
                  <controls:SvgIcon Width="13" Height="13" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="0,2,0,0"
                                    Data="{Binding GeometryKey, Converter={x:Static app:IconGeometryConverter.Instance}}">
                    <controls:SvgIcon.Foreground>
                      <MultiBinding Converter="{x:Static app:IconBrushConverter.Instance}">
                        <Binding Path="BrushKey" />
                        <Binding ElementName="ImportRoot" Path="ActualThemeVariant" />
                      </MultiBinding>
                    </controls:SvgIcon.Foreground>
                  </controls:SvgIcon>
                  <!-- The message carries the severity colour too, exactly as MessageBanner does — the
                       whole point of the shared map is that a finding reads the same wherever it shows. -->
                  <TextBlock Text="{Binding Message}" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="900">
                    <TextBlock.Foreground>
                      <MultiBinding Converter="{x:Static app:IconBrushConverter.Instance}">
                        <Binding Path="BrushKey" />
                        <Binding ElementName="ImportRoot" Path="ActualThemeVariant" />
                      </MultiBinding>
                    </TextBlock.Foreground>
                  </TextBlock>
                </StackPanel>
              </Button>
            </DataTemplate>
          </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
        </ItemsControl>

        <!-- "… and N more problems" — the strip admits it cut the list, and gives it back in one click. -->
        <Button Classes="flat" Padding="2,1" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                IsVisible="{Binding Readiness.HasHiddenItems}"
                ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReadyExpandTooltip}"
                Command="{Binding Readiness.ToggleExpandedCommand}">
          <TextBlock Text="{Binding Readiness.MoreText}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="12" />
        </Button>
      </StackPanel>
    </Border>

    <!-- ══ Band E1 — SOURCE tile (§3.3) ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         One row in the settled state: the picker is ALWAYS live, only the format options fold. -->
    <Border Grid.Row="3" Background="{DynamicResource PanelBrush}"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="0,0,0,1" Padding="12,6">
      <StackPanel x:Name="SourceTile" Spacing="5" DataContext="{Binding Source}" x:DataType="vm:ImportSourceSectionViewModel">

        <!-- The always-live row. -->
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
          <RadioButton Grid.Column="0" GroupName="ImportSourceKind"
                       Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportSourceFile}"
                       IsChecked="{Binding UseFile, Mode=TwoWay}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
          <TextBox Grid.Column="1" x:Name="SourcePathBox" Text="{Binding FilePath, Mode=TwoWay}"
                   IsEnabled="{Binding UseFile}" FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
          <Button Grid.Column="2" Classes="icon" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                  IsEnabled="{Binding UseFile}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportSourceBrowseTooltip}"
                  Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:DataImportTabViewModel)DataContext).BrowseCommand}">
            <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.Folder}"
                              Foreground="{DynamicResource AccentIconBrush}" />
          </Button>
          <!-- Choosing the clipboard READS it: the command points the surface at the clipboard and runs the one
               recalculation chain with a Refresh trigger. The tooltip says so, because a control with a side
               effect should announce it rather than let the user find out. -->
          <RadioButton Grid.Column="3" GroupName="ImportSourceKind"
                       Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportSourceClipboard}"
                       IsChecked="{Binding !UseFile}" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportSourceUseClipboardTooltip}"
                       Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:DataImportTabViewModel)DataContext).UseClipboardCommand}" />

          <!-- Format options disclosure — the debugger launch panel's idiom (chevron + title, no Expander). -->
          <Button Grid.Column="4" Classes="flat" Padding="6,2" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportFormatOptionsTooltip}"
                  Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:DataImportTabViewModel)DataContext).ToggleFormatOptionsCommand}">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
              <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.ChevronRight}" Width="14" Height="14"
                                VerticalAlignment="Center" IsVisible="{Binding !IsExpanded}" />
              <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.ChevronDown}" Width="14" Height="14"
                                VerticalAlignment="Center" IsVisible="{Binding IsExpanded}" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportFormatOptionsHeader}"
                         FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
            </StackPanel>
          </Button>
        </Grid>

        <!-- The thin facts line: what the source is, and how it is being read. Both are read-only statements,
             so they share one subtle row instead of two full-height ones. For the clipboard the facts carry the
             READ TIME, which is what tells the user whether a live source is current. -->
        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6" IsVisible="{Binding !IsExpanded}">
          <TextBlock Text="{Binding SourceFacts}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="11"
                     IsVisible="{Binding SourceFacts, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}" />
          <TextBlock Text="·" Classes="subtle" FontSize="11"
                     IsVisible="{Binding SourceFacts, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}" />
          <TextBlock Text="{Binding SummaryText}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="11"
                     TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- ── The folding half: parsing | culture, side by side (§3.3) ─────────────────────────
             Fields that are always read together share a ROW (U7): densifying horizontally costs no
             control height, which is what the module is allowed to change. Control heights themselves
             belong to the app-wide UX sprint, not here. -->
        <Grid x:Name="FormatOptionsPane" ColumnDefinitions="*,10,*" IsVisible="{Binding IsExpanded}">

          <!-- ── Parsing: HOW THE FILE IS READ ──
               The two groups are cards, not captions: one subject per card, so "how the text is
               read" and "how the values are interpreted" are told apart by looking, not by
               inferring where one caption stops applying. -->
          <Border Grid.Column="0" Classes="settings-group">
          <StackPanel Spacing="5">
            <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportParsingHeader}" Classes="group-header" />

            <!-- ⭐ Sheet picker — shown when the PROVIDER says the source has sheets, never when a file
                 extension says so (§3.3). The whole spreadsheet variant of this card is these two rows plus
                 the row window below, which both variants share. -->
            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8" IsVisible="{Binding SupportsSheets}">
              <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportSheetLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <ComboBox Grid.Column="1" ItemsSource="{Binding Sheets}"
                        SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedSheet, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Name}"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Left" MinWidth="220" FontSize="12" />
            </Grid>

            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto"
                  ColumnSpacing="8" RowSpacing="4">
              <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportDelimiterLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         IsVisible="{Binding SupportsDelimiters}" />
              <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8"
                          IsVisible="{Binding SupportsDelimiters}">
                <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding DelimiterOptions}" SelectedItem="{Binding Delimiter, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}" Width="110" FontSize="12" />
                <CheckBox Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportAutoDetectLabel}"
                          IsChecked="{Binding AutoDetectDelimiter, Mode=TwoWay}" FontSize="11"
                          VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              </StackPanel>

              <!-- The evidence behind the proposal — an automat that explains itself earns trust. -->
              <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding DelimiterEvidence}"
                         Classes="subtle" FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                         IsVisible="{Binding DelimiterEvidence, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}" />

              <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportEncodingLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         IsVisible="{Binding SupportsEncoding}" />
              <StackPanel Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8"
                          IsVisible="{Binding SupportsEncoding}">
                <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding EncodingOptions}" SelectedItem="{Binding Encoding, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}" Width="110" FontSize="12" />
                <CheckBox Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportAutoDetectLabel}"
                          IsChecked="{Binding AutoDetectEncoding, Mode=TwoWay}" FontSize="11"
                          VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              </StackPanel>

              <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding EncodingEvidence}"
                         Classes="subtle" FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                         IsVisible="{Binding EncodingEvidence, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}" />
            </Grid>

            <!-- Qualifier + line ending: two narrow pickers that are always read together. -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" IsVisible="{Binding SupportsDelimiters}">
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportQuoteLabel}" Classes="field-label"
                         VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding QuoteOptions}" SelectedItem="{Binding Quote, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}" Width="70" FontSize="12" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportLineEndingLabel}" Classes="field-label"
                         VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding LineEndingOptions}" SelectedItem="{Binding LineEnding, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}" Width="90" FontSize="12" />
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- Row window: header flag and the first/last row bounds describe one thing. -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
              <CheckBox Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportHasHeaderLabel}"
                        IsChecked="{Binding HasHeader, Mode=TwoWay}" FontSize="12"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportFirstDataRowLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <NumericUpDown Value="{Binding FirstDataRow, Mode=TwoWay}"
                             Minimum="1" Increment="1" Width="90" FontSize="12" FormatString="0" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportLastRowLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <TextBox Text="{Binding LastRowText, Mode=TwoWay}" Width="100" FontSize="12"
                       PlaceholderText="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportLastRowPlaceholder}" />
            </StackPanel>

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" IsVisible="{Binding SupportsDelimiters}">
              <CheckBox Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTrimWhitespaceLabel}"
                        IsChecked="{Binding TrimWhitespace, Mode=TwoWay}" FontSize="12"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNullTokenLabel}" Classes="field-label"
                         VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <TextBox Text="{Binding NullToken, Mode=TwoWay}" Width="110" FontSize="12"
                       PlaceholderText="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNullTokenPlaceholder}" />
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- The spreadsheet's own value question: a date cell is a NUMBER plus a date format, and nothing
                 else distinguishes it (I0 / R3). Turning this off shows the raw Excel serial. -->
            <CheckBox Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportDatesAsDatesLabel}"
                      IsChecked="{Binding DatesAsDates, Mode=TwoWay}" FontSize="12"
                      IsVisible="{Binding SupportsSheets}" />
          </StackPanel>
          </Border>

          <!-- ── Culture: HOW THE VALUES ARE INTERPRETED. Declared, never sniffed (§0.4) ──
               Pairs that are read together share a row, so this went from five rows to three. -->
          <Border Grid.Column="2" Classes="settings-group">
          <StackPanel Spacing="5">
            <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportCultureHeader}" Classes="group-header" />

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportDecimalSeparatorLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding DecimalSeparatorOptions}"
                        SelectedItem="{Binding DecimalSeparator, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}" Width="80" FontSize="12" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportThousandsSeparatorLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding ThousandsSeparatorOptions}"
                        SelectedItem="{Binding ThousandsSeparator, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}" Width="90" FontSize="12" />
            </StackPanel>

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportDateOrderLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding DateOrderOptions}" SelectedItem="{Binding DateOrder, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}" Width="150" FontSize="12" />
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportDateSeparatorLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding DateSeparatorOptions}"
                        SelectedItem="{Binding DateSeparator, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}" Width="80" FontSize="12" />
            </StackPanel>

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
              <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTimeSeparatorLabel}"
                         Classes="field-label" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding TimeSeparatorOptions}"
                        SelectedItem="{Binding TimeSeparator, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}" Width="80" FontSize="12" />
            </StackPanel>
          </StackPanel>
          </Border>
        </Grid>
      </StackPanel>
    </Border>

    <!-- ══ Band E2 — TARGET tile (§3.4) ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         Two variants, one tile, read top-down: an EXISTING table has a shape to obey, a NEW one has a
         shape to choose. Only the chosen variant's detail occupies space, so the tile stays one thin
         line until there is something to say — the star row still belongs to the WORK (§3.1), which is
         why the type grid is height-capped and scrolls rather than growing without limit. -->
    <Border Grid.Row="4" Background="{DynamicResource PanelBrush}"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="0,0,0,1" Padding="12,6">
      <StackPanel x:Name="TargetTile" Spacing="5" DataContext="{Binding Target}" x:DataType="vm:ImportTargetSectionViewModel">

        <!-- ── The target CHOICE: two variants, ONE grid ─────────────────────────────────────────
             ⭐ One grid rather than two stacked ones, because the two radios are a single choice and have
             to read as one. Sharing the column definitions is what does it: the radio column sizes to the
             wider of the two labels, so both inputs start at the SAME x — as two separate grids they each
             measured their own label and the inputs sat a few pixels apart, which is what made the pair
             look ragged and unrelated. The facts line moved out from BETWEEN them (it was splitting the
             choice in half and spending a row on it) to below the pair, where it belongs to the answer
             rather than to the question. -->
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto,Auto" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto"
              ColumnSpacing="8" RowSpacing="3">

          <RadioButton Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" GroupName="ImportTargetKind"
                       Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTargetExistingTable}"
                       IsChecked="{Binding IsExistingTable, Mode=TwoWay}"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" FontSize="12" />

          <controls:SearchableComboBox Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" x:Name="TargetPicker"
                                       ItemsSource="{Binding Tables}"
                                       SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedTable, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       IsEnabled="{Binding IsExistingTable}"
                                       Watermark="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTargetTableWatermark}"
                                       FilterWatermark="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTargetFilterWatermark}"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Left" MinWidth="360" />

          <CheckBox Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="2" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTargetEmptyFirst}"
                    ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTargetEmptyFirstTooltip}"
                    IsVisible="{Binding IsExistingTable}"
                    IsChecked="{Binding EmptyBeforeImport, Mode=TwoWay}" FontSize="12" />

          <RadioButton Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" GroupName="ImportTargetKind"
                       Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTargetNewTable}"
                       IsChecked="{Binding IsNewTable, Mode=TwoWay}"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" FontSize="12" />

          <TextBox Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" x:Name="NewTableNameBox"
                   Text="{Binding NewTableName, Mode=TwoWay}"
                   IsEnabled="{Binding IsNewTable}"
                   PlaceholderText="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportTargetNewTableWatermark}"
                   HorizontalAlignment="Left" MinWidth="360" FontSize="12" />

          <!-- ⚠ §0.5: the CREATE is committed before the first row (gotcha #213), so this is the only
               way to undo it — and it is off by default, like every option that destroys something. -->
          <CheckBox Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="2" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableDropOnFailure}"
                    ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableDropOnFailureTooltip}"
                    IsVisible="{Binding IsNewTable}"
                    IsChecked="{Binding DropTableOnFailure, Mode=TwoWay}" FontSize="12" />

          <!-- „Show DDL" moved to the Table types panel with the preview it toggles — a toggle in one band
               and the thing it reveals in another is how a control stops looking connected to anything. -->
        </Grid>

        <TextBlock Text="{Binding FactsText}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="11"
                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                   IsVisible="{Binding FactsText, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}" />

        <!-- ⭐ The type grid, its basis line and the DDL preview used to hang HERE, under the choice, which
             made this Auto band the tallest thing on the surface in the „new table" variant and left the work
             area with whatever was over. They moved into the work area (band F) in the configuration/results
             split of 2026-07-27: the columns about to be created are a CONFIGURATION decision, so they belong
             beside Mapping, not above it. What stays here is the choice itself and the facts about it. -->
      </StackPanel>
    </Border>

    <!-- ══ Band F — the work area: THE CONFIGURATION, at full height ════════════════════════════
         ⭐ Ratified 2026-07-27 — the split that reorganised the whole surface: **the top half is where the
         import is DESIGNED, the bottom panel is where RESULTS land.** Before it, „Preview after conversion"
         (a result — what the pipeline produces) sat in the work area competing for space with Mapping (a
         decision), while the type grid — also a decision — sat above in an Auto band. Configuration and
         outcome were interleaved and fought over the same pixels.

         Now:
           • EXISTING table → the work area is Mapping, full width. Nothing to share it with.
           • NEW table      → Table types | Mapping, split by a draggable splitter, so the user sets the
                              proportion. Both halves are configuration; both are about the same import.
           • either way     → the converted preview is a BOTTOM TAB beside Source preview / Errors / Report.

         The column widths are re-normalized in ONE place (ApplyWorkAreaLayout), the way the bottom panel's
         rows are — a splitter turns a star column into absolute pixels the moment it is dragged, so a
         variant switch has to set BOTH columns or the layout keeps whatever the last drag left (#240). -->
    <Grid Grid.Row="5" x:Name="WorkArea" ColumnDefinitions="*,4,*">

      <!-- ── The new table's columns: the left half, and only in that variant ───────────────────── -->
      <Grid Grid.Column="0" x:Name="TypesPanel" Margin="12,8" RowDefinitions="Auto,*"
            DataContext="{Binding Target}" x:DataType="vm:ImportTargetSectionViewModel"
            IsVisible="{Binding IsNewTable}">

        <!-- Title + the basis, in the same shape Mapping and the preview use: a title says what the region
             IS, the subtle line beside it says how it currently stands. -->
        <!-- ⚠ No „Show DDL" button. The generated statement is a bottom TAB now, always current — so there is
             no disclosure to toggle, nothing to navigate to, and no state saying whether it is on screen. -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8" Margin="0,0,0,6">
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableTypesTitle}"
                     Classes="group-header" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0" />
          <!-- ⭐ Always visible (§3.4): the number of rows the types rest on. REK-7 makes that the WHOLE
               source, and a type is worth exactly as much as the evidence behind it. -->
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding InferenceBasisText}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="12"
                     VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
        </Grid>

        <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableEmpty}"
                   Classes="subtle" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="560"
                   HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                   IsVisible="{Binding !HasNewColumns}" />

        <!-- ⭐ The grid is EDITABLE, not merely shown (§0.3). Once the CREATE has run the table is
             committed and beyond a Rollback, so this is the last moment a wrong type costs nothing.
             ⚠ It fills the panel: no wrapper row for the DDL (which is not here any more) and no MaxHeight
             on the scroller. Both mattered — the cap SURVIVED the move to the work area for one round, and
             a Stretch-aligned control that cannot use its space gets CENTRED in it, so the grid floated with
             blank bands above and below while every property looked correct. -->
        <Border Grid.Row="1" IsVisible="{Binding HasNewColumns}"
                BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="3">
            <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*">

              <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnSpacing="8" Margin="8,5"
                    Background="{DynamicResource ChromeStrongBrush}">
                <!-- ⚠⚠ Szerokość kolumny "Basis" MUSI reagować na jej widoczność. Ukryty TextBlock znika,
                     ale ColumnDefinition dalej mierzy swoje 3* — zgłoszenie QA („kolumna Column ma za mało
                     miejsca") miało przyczynę OBOK: przy imporcie bez per-kolumnowej podstawy jedna trzecia
                     siatki stała pusta. ColumnDefinition nie ma `IsVisible`, więc reaguje sama szerokość. -->
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="5*" />
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="3*" />
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="62" />
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="62" />
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" MinWidth="32" />
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding HasPerColumnBasis, Converter={x:Static conv:BoolToStarWidthConverter.Instance}, ConverterParameter=3}" />
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableColumnName}"
                           Classes="field-label" Margin="0" />
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableColumnType}"
                           Classes="field-label" Margin="0" />
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableColumnSize}"
                           Classes="field-label" Margin="0" />
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableColumnScale}"
                           Classes="field-label" Margin="0" />
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="4" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableColumnNullable}"
                           Classes="field-label" Margin="0" HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                <!-- ⭐ The caption goes with its cells. When every column shares one basis it is said once on
                     the section's line above, and a column header naming an empty column would be exactly the
                     kind of thing that reads as a control with nothing behind it. -->
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="5" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportNewTableColumnBasis}"
                           Classes="field-label" Margin="0"
                           IsVisible="{Binding HasPerColumnBasis}" />
              </Grid>

              <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="1">
                <ItemsControl x:Name="NewTableColumnRows" ItemsSource="{Binding NewColumns}">
                  <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ImportNewTableColumnRowViewModel">
                      <Grid ColumnSpacing="8" Margin="8,3">
                        <!-- ⚠ Identyczna definicja jak w nagłówku — obie muszą się zgadzać co do znaku. -->
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                          <ColumnDefinition Width="5*" />
                          <ColumnDefinition Width="3*" />
                          <ColumnDefinition Width="62" />
                          <ColumnDefinition Width="62" />
                          <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" MinWidth="32" />
                          <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding $parent[ItemsControl].((vm:ImportTargetSectionViewModel)DataContext).HasPerColumnBasis, Converter={x:Static conv:BoolToStarWidthConverter.Instance}, ConverterParameter=3}" />
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                        <TextBox Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding Name, Mode=TwoWay}" FontSize="12" />

                        <ComboBox Grid.Column="1" ItemsSource="{Binding TypeOptions}"
                                  SelectedItem="{Binding Type, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                  HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" FontSize="12" />

                        <!-- Size and Scale are enabled by the SHARED FieldTypeRules, so "does VARCHAR
                             take a length" has one answer app-wide (§4.6). -->
                        <NumericUpDown Grid.Column="2" Value="{Binding Size, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       IsEnabled="{Binding IsSizeEnabled}" ShowButtonSpinner="False"
                                       Minimum="1" FormatString="0" FontSize="12" />
                        <NumericUpDown Grid.Column="3" Value="{Binding Scale, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       IsEnabled="{Binding IsScaleEnabled}" ShowButtonSpinner="False"
                                       Minimum="0" FormatString="0" FontSize="12" />

                        <!-- ⚠ Wyśrodkowany w poziomie: dosunięty do lewej zostawiał po prawej pustkę,
                             którą użytkownik odczytał jako „kolumna NULL ma bardzo dużo wolnego miejsca". -->
                        <CheckBox Grid.Column="4" IsChecked="{Binding IsNullable, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                  VerticalAlignment="Center" HorizontalAlignment="Center" />

                        <!-- ⭐ "Basis" answers "where did that type come from" — and for a mixed column
                             (R19, the measured norm) it names the value and the row that decided it, so
                             the user can check their own file rather than take our word (§0.6).
                             ⚠ One line, trimmed, with the full sentence on hover: wrapping made a long
                             basis two or three lines tall, which set the height of its whole row and let
                             the explanation dominate the grid it was only annotating. Trimming changes
                             nothing about what is available — the text is one hover away, and §0.6 is
                             about the evidence being reachable, not about it being the widest thing on
                             screen. -->
                        <TextBlock Grid.Column="5" Text="{Binding Basis}" FontSize="11"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                   ToolTip.Tip="{Binding Basis}"
                                   IsVisible="{Binding $parent[ItemsControl].((vm:ImportTargetSectionViewModel)DataContext).HasPerColumnBasis}"
                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}" />
                      </Grid>
                    </DataTemplate>
                  </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                </ItemsControl>
              </ScrollViewer>
            </Grid>
          </Border>

          <!-- ⚠ Two things used to sit HERE and both are gone, for the same reason in two sizes: one screen
               should say a thing once, and a panel should hold only what is being worked on.

               §0.5's sentence ("this CREATE is committed and a rollback will not remove it") was a second
               banner repeating what the readiness strip already carries as IMP0018 — from Core, and naming
               the table besides.

               The generated CREATE TABLE was disclosed inline. It is consulted rarely, yet its panel
               complicated this column permanently: the types grid shared its space with something almost
               always empty. „Show DDL" now opens the statement in the SQL Editor, where it can be read,
               edited and run — and where it costs nothing until it is asked for. -->
      </Grid>

      <!-- Only there when there is a left half to divide. -->
      <GridSplitter Grid.Column="1" x:Name="WorkSplitter" ResizeDirection="Columns" Width="4"
                    VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Background="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}"
                    IsVisible="{Binding Target.IsNewTable}" />

    <Grid Grid.Column="2" x:Name="MappingPanel" Margin="12,8" DataContext="{Binding Mapping}" x:DataType="vm:ImportMappingPanelViewModel">

      <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingEmpty}"
                 Classes="subtle" FontSize="12" MaxWidth="560"
                 HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                 IsVisible="{Binding !HasTarget}" />

      <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" IsVisible="{Binding HasTarget}">

        <!-- Title + headline + the two re-plan strategies + the filter.
             ⭐ The TITLE is new and it is why this row changed shape: the preview half already had one and
             this half had only its dynamic headline, so the work area read as one undivided surface with a
             status line floating in it. Both halves now name themselves the same way, with the same weight
             (the shared `group-header`), and the dynamic count stays subtle beside the name — a title says
             what the region IS, a headline says how it is doing. -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8" Margin="0,0,0,6">
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingTitle}"
                     Classes="group-header" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0" />
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Headline}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="12"
                     VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
          <Button Grid.Column="2" Classes="flat" FontSize="12"
                  Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingMatchByPosition}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingMatchByPositionTooltip}"
                  Command="{Binding MatchByPositionCommand}" />
          <Button Grid.Column="3" Classes="flat" FontSize="12"
                  Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingClear}"
                  Command="{Binding ClearMappingCommand}" />
          <CheckBox Grid.Column="4" VerticalAlignment="Center" FontSize="12"
                    Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingOnlyUnmapped}"
                    IsChecked="{Binding ShowOnlyUnmapped, Mode=TwoWay}" />
        </Grid>

        <!-- The grid. Orientation is TARGET → SOURCE: the target column is the side with requirements
             (NOT NULL, a type, a length); the source field is the choice (§3.5). -->
        <Border Grid.Row="1" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="3">
          <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*">

            <!-- Column captions. Same proportions as the rows below, so they stay aligned. -->
            <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="2*,3*,2*,3*" ColumnSpacing="10" Margin="8,5"
                  Background="{DynamicResource ChromeStrongBrush}">
              <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingColumnTarget}"
                         Classes="field-label" Margin="0" />
              <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingColumnSource}"
                         Classes="field-label" Margin="0" />
              <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingColumnType}"
                         Classes="field-label" Margin="0" />
              <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingColumnNote}"
                         Classes="field-label" Margin="0" />
            </Grid>

            <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="1">
            <ItemsControl x:Name="MappingRows" ItemsSource="{Binding VisibleRows}">
              <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ImportMappingRowViewModel">
                  <Grid ColumnDefinitions="2*,3*,2*,3*" ColumnSpacing="10" Margin="8,4">

                    <!-- Target column. A required column says so, because leaving it unmapped BLOCKS the
                         import rather than merely warning. -->
                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="4" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                      <TextBlock Text="{Binding TargetColumnName}" FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                 TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                      <TextBlock Text="*" FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                 Foreground="{DynamicResource ErrorBrush}"
                                 IsVisible="{Binding IsRequired}" />
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- Source field + the identity unlock, which is the only way a GENERATED ALWAYS
                         column becomes mappable (R10).
                         ⚠ A GRID, not a StackPanel, and the ComboBox carries NO MinWidth: a StackPanel does
                         not constrain its children, so a picker with a minimum width wider than the column
                         simply overflowed into the "Target type" column beside it. The star column makes the
                         picker shrink instead — each column keeps its own space. -->
                    <Grid Grid.Column="1" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                      <ComboBox Grid.Column="0"
                                ItemsSource="{Binding Options}"
                                SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                DisplayMemberBinding="{Binding Display}"
                                IsEnabled="{Binding IsPickerEnabled}"
                                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" FontSize="12" />
                      <CheckBox Grid.Column="1"
                                Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportMappingUnlockIdentity}"
                                IsChecked="{Binding IsIdentityUnlocked, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                IsVisible="{Binding NeedsIdentityOverride}"
                                ToolTip.Tip="{Binding LockReason}"
                                FontSize="11" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                      <!-- Origin, in the debugger's ValueOrigin vocabulary: "matched" is quiet because it
                           rests on a provable fact; "assumed" is an ACCENT — worth a look, not an error. -->
                      <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding OriginText}" FontSize="11"
                                 VerticalAlignment="Center" FontStyle="Italic"
                                 Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}"
                                 IsVisible="{Binding IsAutomatic}" />
                      <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding OriginText}" FontSize="11"
                                 VerticalAlignment="Center" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                 Foreground="{DynamicResource AccentBrush}"
                                 IsVisible="{Binding IsAssumed}" />
                    </Grid>

                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding TypeText}" FontSize="12"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}" />

                    <!-- The note: either why the column is locked, or what the planner said about it.
                         Both are reasons, and a blocked control without one is a UX defect (§9.1.3). -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" FontSize="11" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                               TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               Text="{Binding LockReason}"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding !IsPickerEnabled}" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" FontSize="11" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                               TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               Text="{Binding DiagnosticText}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding HasDiagnostic}">
                      <TextBlock.Foreground>
                        <MultiBinding Converter="{x:Static app:IconBrushConverter.Instance}">
                          <Binding Path="DiagnosticBrushKey" />
                          <Binding ElementName="ImportRoot" Path="ActualThemeVariant" />
                        </MultiBinding>
                      </TextBlock.Foreground>
                    </TextBlock>
                  </Grid>
                </DataTemplate>
              </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            </ItemsControl>
            </ScrollViewer>
          </Grid>
        </Border>

        <!-- The source fields nobody consumes — how "I forgot a column" becomes visible BEFORE the
             import instead of after it. -->
        <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Text="{Binding UnusedFieldsText}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="11"
                   Margin="0,6,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                   IsVisible="{Binding HasUnusedFields}" />
      </Grid>
    </Grid>

    </Grid>

    <!-- ══ The bottom panel's splitter (U2) ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         Always visible while the surface is — deliberately NOT bound to !IsBottomPanelCollapsed, which is
         the state its own double-click toggles; binding a splitter's visibility to what it toggles is
         gotcha #240 part 3, and it cost three commits in the debugger. -->
    <GridSplitter Grid.Row="6" x:Name="BottomSplitter" Height="4"
                  ResizeDirection="Rows" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                  Background="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" />

    <!-- ══ Band G — bottom tabs. Collapse renormalizes BOTH grid rows (gotcha #240). ═════════════
         Three tabs, one question each: what the file HOLDS (raw records), what the CURRENT settings
         would reject (found without running anything), and what a run actually DID. The Errors tab
         carries its count — a tab that hides how much it has to say has to be opened to find out.
         The chevron overlays the strip and the tab CONTENTS carry the collapse binding, exactly as in
         the debugger, so a collapsed panel measures down to the strip alone. -->
    <Border Grid.Row="7" ClipToBounds="True" Background="{DynamicResource PanelBrush}"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="0,1,0,0"
            DoubleTapped="OnBottomPanelDoubleTapped">
      <Grid>
        <Button Classes="icon" ZIndex="1"
                HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="0,2,6,0"
                ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportBottomPanelToggleTooltip}"
                Command="{Binding ToggleBottomPanelCommand}">
          <Panel>
            <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.ChevronsDown}" Width="14" Height="14"
                              Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}"
                              IsVisible="{Binding !IsBottomPanelCollapsed}" />
            <controls:SvgIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.ChevronsUp}" Width="14" Height="14"
                              Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}"
                              IsVisible="{Binding IsBottomPanelCollapsed}" />
          </Panel>
        </Button>

        <TabControl x:Name="BottomTabs" Padding="0">

          <!-- ── Source preview: the provider's own records, before anything was converted ── -->
          <TabItem Classes="bottom-tab" Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportSourcePreviewTab}">
          <Grid IsVisible="{Binding !IsBottomPanelCollapsed}">
            <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportSourcePreviewEmpty}"
                       Classes="subtle" Margin="12,10" FontSize="12"
                       IsVisible="{Binding !PreviewRows.Count}" />
            <DataGrid x:Name="SourcePreviewGrid"
                      ItemsSource="{Binding PreviewRows}"
                      IsVisible="{Binding PreviewRows.Count}"
                      IsReadOnly="True"
                      AutoGenerateColumns="False"
                      HeadersVisibility="Column"
                      GridLinesVisibility="All"
                      CanUserSortColumns="False"
                      FontSize="12" />
          </Grid>
          </TabItem>

          <!-- ── Preview after conversion (§3.6) — "exactly what reaches the database" ──────────────
               ⭐ It lives HERE, not in the work area, since the configuration/results split of 2026-07-27.
               It is a RESULT — what the pipeline produces from the current settings — and it is needed in
               both target variants, so putting it beside Mapping made a decision and its consequence fight
               over the same pixels while the work area lost half its width to it. The bottom panel is where
               outcomes belong, next to Source preview, Errors and Report.

               Filled by the REAL pipeline (bounded provider + a writer that keeps rows instead of sending
               them), which is the only way §3.6's claim can be true.
               ⛔ The shared filter panel and the aggregation bar are deliberately NOT wired: a filter here
                  would suggest it changes what gets imported. Filtering before import is its own planned
                  feature (§9.5) — a boundary, not an oversight. -->
          <TabItem Classes="bottom-tab" Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportPreviewTitle}">
          <Panel IsVisible="{Binding !IsBottomPanelCollapsed}">
          <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*" Margin="12,8"
                DataContext="{Binding ConvertedPreview}" x:DataType="vm:ImportConvertedPreviewViewModel">

            <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Text="{Binding Headline}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="12"
                       Margin="0,0,0,6" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                       IsVisible="{Binding HasRows}" />

            <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportPreviewEmpty}"
                       Classes="subtle" FontSize="12" MaxWidth="420" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                       IsVisible="{Binding !HasRows}" />

            <Border Grid.Row="1" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="3"
                    IsVisible="{Binding HasRows}">
              <DataGrid x:Name="ConvertedPreviewGrid"
                        ItemsSource="{Binding Rows}"
                        IsReadOnly="True"
                        AutoGenerateColumns="False"
                        HeadersVisibility="Column"
                        GridLinesVisibility="All"
                        CanUserSortColumns="False"
                        FontSize="12" />
            </Border>
          </Grid>
          </Panel>
          </TabItem>

          <!-- ── Errors: what the CURRENT settings would reject, found without running anything ──
               Same row type and same four columns as the report's list — one problem reads the same
               wherever it is shown. -->
          <TabItem Classes="bottom-tab" Header="{Binding ConvertedPreview.ProblemsTabHeader}">
          <Grid IsVisible="{Binding !IsBottomPanelCollapsed}">
            <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportErrorsEmpty}"
                       Classes="subtle" Margin="12,10" FontSize="12"
                       IsVisible="{Binding !ConvertedPreview.HasProblems}" />
            <DataGrid ItemsSource="{Binding ConvertedPreview.Problems}"
                      IsVisible="{Binding ConvertedPreview.HasProblems}"
                      IsReadOnly="True" AutoGenerateColumns="False" HeadersVisibility="Column"
                      GridLinesVisibility="All" CanUserSortColumns="False" FontSize="12"
                      DoubleTapped="OnProblemDoubleTapped">
              <DataGrid.Columns>
                <DataGridTextColumn Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportColumnRow}"
                                    Binding="{Binding SourceRowNumber}" IsReadOnly="True" />
                <DataGridTextColumn Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportColumnColumn}"
                                    Binding="{Binding ColumnName}" IsReadOnly="True" />
                <DataGridTextColumn Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportColumnValue}"
                                    Binding="{Binding RawValue}" IsReadOnly="True" />
                <DataGridTextColumn Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportColumnReason}"
                                    Binding="{Binding Reason}" IsReadOnly="True" Width="*" />
              </DataGrid.Columns>
            </DataGrid>
          </Grid>
          </TabItem>

          <!-- ── Report: what a run DID, and the transaction decision beside the numbers (§3.7) ── -->
          <TabItem Classes="bottom-tab" Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportTab}">
          <Panel IsVisible="{Binding !IsBottomPanelCollapsed}">
          <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*"
                DataContext="{Binding Report}" x:DataType="vm:ImportRunReportViewModel">

            <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportEmpty}"
                       Classes="subtle" Margin="12,10" FontSize="12"
                       IsVisible="{Binding !HasReport}" />

            <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Spacing="4" Margin="12,8" IsVisible="{Binding HasReport}">
              <!-- The headline carries the severity colour through the shared MessageBanner table, so the
                   report describes a state the same way every other surface does (§9.3). -->
              <TextBlock Text="{Binding Headline}" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <TextBlock.Foreground>
                  <MultiBinding Converter="{x:Static app:IconBrushConverter.Instance}">
                    <Binding Path="SeverityBrushKey" />
                    <Binding ElementName="ImportRoot" Path="ActualThemeVariant" />
                  </MultiBinding>
                </TextBlock.Foreground>
              </TextBlock>

              <TextBlock Text="{Binding Note}" Classes="subtle" FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                         IsVisible="{Binding HasNote}" />

              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" Margin="0,2,0,0">
                <!-- ⚠ Commit / Rollback are NOT here any more. They moved to the top command bar after the
                     I7 review: in EmberTern every main action is taken from the toolbar, and hiding the
                     transaction decision at the bottom of the window made a successful import read as a
                     failure — the only thing in view was a red "a working transaction is open" line. The
                     Report tab reports; the toolbar acts. -->

                <!-- Export goes through the SHARED export framework — CSV / XLSX / clipboard for free,
                     without one line of new serialization (§4.6). -->
                <Button Classes="flat" FontSize="12"
                        Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportExport}"
                        IsEnabled="{Binding HasProblems}"
                        Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:DataImportTabViewModel)DataContext).ExportReportCommand}" />
                <Button Classes="flat" FontSize="12"
                        Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportCopy}"
                        Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:DataImportTabViewModel)DataContext).CopyReportCommand}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </StackPanel>

            <DataGrid Grid.Row="1" ItemsSource="{Binding Problems}"
                      IsVisible="{Binding HasProblems}"
                      IsReadOnly="True" AutoGenerateColumns="False" HeadersVisibility="Column"
                      GridLinesVisibility="All" CanUserSortColumns="False" FontSize="12"
                      ToolTip.Tip="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportRevealTooltip}"
                      DoubleTapped="OnProblemDoubleTapped">
              <DataGrid.Columns>
                <DataGridTextColumn Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportColumnRow}"
                                    Binding="{Binding SourceRowNumber}" IsReadOnly="True" />
                <DataGridTextColumn Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportColumnColumn}"
                                    Binding="{Binding ColumnName}" IsReadOnly="True" />
                <DataGridTextColumn Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportColumnValue}"
                                    Binding="{Binding RawValue}" IsReadOnly="True" />
                <DataGridTextColumn Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportReportColumnReason}"
                                    Binding="{Binding Reason}" IsReadOnly="True" Width="*" />
              </DataGrid.Columns>
            </DataGrid>
          </Grid>
          </Panel>
          </TabItem>

          <!-- ── DDL: the exact CREATE TABLE this import will run ────────────────────────────────────
               ⭐ A TAB rather than a button, decided after two worse answers. It was first disclosed inline
               in the types column — a panel almost always empty, complicating that column permanently — and
               then briefly opened in the SQL Editor, which was worse in a different way: **the generated DDL
               is part of configuring THIS import, so reaching it must not switch modules or move the active
               tab.** Here it costs no space until selected, never navigates anywhere, and sits with the other
               artefacts of the run.

               Rendered LIVE from `CreateTableSql`, which is computed from the grid above through the same
               `ImportNewTable.BuildCreateSql` the run itself calls — so it cannot go stale and there is no
               refresh to forget. Selectable, so copying it needs no button of its own.

               ⚠ Visible only in the „new table" variant: in the other one there is no statement to generate,
               and a permanently empty tab is a promise nothing keeps. It is LAST on the strip on purpose —
               a hidden tab still occupies its index, and the run reveals the Report by index. -->
          <TabItem Classes="bottom-tab" Header="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportDdlTab}"
                   IsVisible="{Binding Target.IsNewTable}">
          <Panel IsVisible="{Binding !IsBottomPanelCollapsed}">
          <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*" Margin="12,8"
                DataContext="{Binding Target}" x:DataType="vm:ImportTargetSectionViewModel">

            <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportDdlLive}"
                       Classes="subtle" FontSize="11" Margin="0,0,0,6"
                       IsVisible="{Binding CreateTableSql, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}" />

            <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportDdlEmpty}"
                       Classes="subtle" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="480"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                       IsVisible="{Binding CreateTableSql, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNullOrEmpty}}" />

            <!-- ⭐ The SAME read-only SQL surface the other eleven DDL previews use — an AvaloniaEdit
                 TextEditor with `SqlEditorBehavior.AttachReadOnlyHighlighting`, so generated SQL reads
                 identically wherever EmberTern shows it: the shared XSHD lexical layer plus the SEMANTIC
                 accent layer, from the one Lexer/Parser/SemanticModel front-end. Not a second renderer, and
                 not a plain text block that would be the only SQL in the application without colour.
                 ⚠ Read-only in the strict sense the seam guarantees: `AttachReadOnlyHighlighting` deliberately
                 does NOT wire completion, squiggles or typing ergonomics — a preview must not offer to edit
                 what it is only showing. Line numbers are off: this is one short statement, not a document.
                 Its Text is PUSHED from the VM in code-behind (two-way TextEditor.Text binding is flaky —
                 the same gotcha every other DDL preview works around). -->
            <Border Grid.Row="1" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="3"
                    IsVisible="{Binding CreateTableSql, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}">
              <ae:TextEditor x:Name="DdlEditor"
                             ShowLineNumbers="False"
                             IsReadOnly="True"
                             FontFamily="Cascadia Code,Consolas,Menlo,monospace"
                             FontSize="13"
                             HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                             VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                             Background="{DynamicResource BackgroundBrush}"
                             Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundBrush}" />
            </Border>
          </Grid>
          </Panel>
          </TabItem>
        </TabControl>
      </Grid>
    </Border>

    <!-- ══ Band H — where the rows land, then the numbers. Never adjectives (§9.1 point 4) ══════ -->
    <Border Grid.Row="8" Classes="chrome" Background="{DynamicResource ChromeStrongBrush}"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" BorderThickness="0,1,0,0" Padding="12,4">
      <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="10">
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding DestinationStatus}" FontSize="12"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}" />
        <TextBlock Text="│" FontSize="12" Foreground="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" />
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding SurfaceStatus}" FontSize="12"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}" />

        <!-- The quiet restore note (§4.8.4): an automatic restore the user cannot see is a configuration
             they did not choose, so it says so — and offers to forget it in one click. -->
        <TextBlock Text="│" FontSize="12" Foreground="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}"
                   IsVisible="{Binding RestoredLastConfiguration}" />
        <TextBlock Text="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportRestoredLastConfiguration}" FontSize="12"
                   FontStyle="Italic" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}"
                   IsVisible="{Binding RestoredLastConfiguration}" />
        <Button Classes="flat" Padding="4,0" FontSize="11" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                Content="{x:Static app:UiStrings.ImportForgetLastConfiguration}"
                IsVisible="{Binding RestoredLastConfiguration}"
                Command="{Binding ForgetLastConfigurationCommand}" />
      </StackPanel>
    </Border>
  </Grid>
</UserControl>
